      {
        "id": 313285,
        "name": "Fragmented Almanac",
        "summary": "Embark on an enigmatic odyssey through time and space in Fragmented Almanac, a mesmerizing narrative puzzle game redefining retro gaming on the SEGA Dreamcast.\n\nYou will embark on a journey through a complex timeline, exploring The Hideout—a repository of alchemical knowledge, ancient tales, and mystical symbols. As a trapped spirit seeking to reunite with its original body, you will unravel the mysteries of this enigmatic realm.\n\nAdditionally, players will delve into the alternate universe of Summoning Signals, assuming the role of The Pilot aboard the Sprinter-2 ship, which has crash-landed on an Unknown Planet. Amidst a blend of futuristic technology and ancient ruins, players must navigate the labyrinthine landscapes, repairing their ship and unraveling the secrets of this strange world.\n\nAt the junction of video games, new media art and alchemy, this project is the culmination of 7 years of Dreamcast development, spread over 5 different games. Fragmented Almanac is a short but dense experience and offers a modern twist on retro gaming, combining nostalgic aesthetics with innovative gameplay.\n\nAre you ready to uncover the fragments and embark on an enigmatic journey shrouded in mystery?",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co8rq4.jpg",
        "release_date": 1712534400,
        "rating": null,
        "rating_count": null,
        "genres": "Point-and-click|Puzzle|Adventure",
        "platform_ids": "23",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/fragmented-almanac",
        "cached_at": 1772527920
      },
      {
        "id": 313975,
        "name": "Grauen no Torikago: Kapitel 1 - Keiyaku",
        "summary": "Grauen no Torikago: Kapitel 1 - Keiyaku is the first chapter of a horror movie sold exclusively through the Dreamcast Direct online service. The film is divided into 365 episodes, each lasting one minute. It was impossible to watch all the episodes at once as they opened gradually. From 1 October 1999 to 1 October 2000, it was necessary to connect Dreamcast to the internet daily and download special save files on the VMU that opened new episodes.\n\nThe servers went offline shortly after the final episode unlocked. Now it is necessary to use a special VMU save or directly extract the videos of the GDI disc image to watch the film. The sequels of Grauen no Torikago were only available to consumers who had finished previous chapters, making later entries exceedingly rare.\n\nAs of July 2024, a restoration patch has been made by Derek Pascarella that allows you to watch the videos without the vmu save.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co8v3s.jpg",
        "release_date": 938649600,
